       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions, and it's usually given as 600\u2013800 mg three or four times daily.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours**. This is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, such as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still want it reviewed with pharmacy or the prescriber before it's entered.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
